# docs_updater

After meaningful code changes affecting documented behavior, update `/docs/` and (if relevant) the root README.

The full procedure (code → document mapping, **when to add a new ADR vs edit docs**, immutability of accepted ADRs, what to update vs. leave alone, anti-patterns) is in [.claude/skills/docs_updater/SKILL.md](mdc:.claude/skills/docs_updater/SKILL.md).

Read that file when this rule triggers, then follow it.

**Code → docs cheat sheet:**

| Code change | Doc to update |
|---|---|
| New/removed screen | `docs/tech/godot-client.md` (structure, screen flow) |
| New/removed gameplay mode | new file in `docs/design/systems/`, update `docs/design/overview.md` |
| New rule / system in `game/core/` | `docs/tech/godot-client.md` + `docs/design/systems/` |
| New agent tool / protocol message | ADR-0009 «Протокол X.Y», `contract/` |
| Changed system prompt | `docs/tech/llm-integration.md` + relevant `docs/design/systems/<mode>.md` |
| New/changed entity class | `docs/tech/data-models.md` |
| LLM model/provider change | `docs/tech/llm-integration.md` + `README.md` |
| Save format change | `docs/tech/godot-client.md` §«Сейвы» |
| Removing legacy | scrub mentions everywhere + mark in `docs/production/backlog.md` |
| New architectural decision | new ADR in `docs/tech/adr/NNNN-<topic>.md` |
| Roadmap pillar closed | mark `[x]` in `docs/production/roadmap.md`, move item in `backlog.md` |

**Do NOT** update `RELEASE_NOTES.md` here — that's a separate flow (see `release_notes_updater` rule).
